<!-- §01 THE DISTILLATION TRAP -->
<section id="s-trap" data-code="trap">
<div class="section-no">01 — The Distillation Trap</div>
<h2>Why "Better Benchmarks" Isn't Enough</h2>
<p>The dominant recipe for building a strong vision-language model today is straightforward: use a proprietary black-box model — GPT-4o, Gemini, Claude — to label your training data, then train on those labels. Benchmarks go up. Papers get published. But here's the problem: you have no idea <em>why</em> they went up.</p>
<p>Did your architecture improve? Did your training procedure help? Or did GPT-4o already memorize the evaluation set during its own training? You can't tell. Worse, the community builds on this work without knowing whether it represents genuine progress or just proprietary data laundering.</p>

<div class="vp">
  <div class="vp-head">
    <span class="vp-title">two training philosophies</span>
    <span class="vp-hint">closed vs open</span>
  </div>
  <div class="vp-body" style="padding:0">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 620 220" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" style="width:100%;display:block">
      <defs>
        <marker id="arr" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="6" refX="8" refY="3" orient="auto">
          <polygon points="0 0, 8 3, 0 6" fill="#5c6370"/>
        </marker>
        <marker id="arr-p" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="6" refX="8" refY="3" orient="auto">
          <polygon points="0 0, 8 3, 0 6" fill="#8b5cf6"/>
        </marker>
      </defs>
      <!-- LEFT: Distillation path -->
      <text x="155" y="22" text-anchor="middle" font-family="monospace" font-size="10" fill="#6b7280" letter-spacing="2">DISTILLATION PATH</text>
