<div class="listen-friendly-content" style="display:none" aria-hidden="true">
  <div lang="en">
    <h2>Audio Summary: PerceptionLM — Open Video Understanding Without Black-Box Distillation</h2>
    <p>PerceptionLM, or PLM, is Meta FAIR's fully open and reproducible vision-language model for image and video understanding. Unlike most competitive VLMs that use proprietary models like GPT-4o to label training data — a process called distillation — PLM is built entirely from open-access data and transparent methods, making scientific progress measurable.</p>
    <p>The key finding is that synthetic data scaling works well for standard video tasks but completely fails for fine-grained video understanding, showing a power law exponent of negative 0.03 versus negative 0.15 for standard tasks — five times flatter. To fill this gap, the authors release 2.4 million human-labeled fine-grained video QA pairs called PLM-FGQA, covering movement direction, counting, spatial relationships, and other detailed question types that existing datasets severely undercount. They also release PLM-STC, 476,000 spatio-temporal captions paired with masklets — pixel-level segmentation masks that track subjects through video — enabling spatial and temporal grounding. Together, these datasets push PLM-8B to 55.6 on the new PLM-VideoBench, surpassing GPT-4o at 51.6 and InternVL2.5 at 38.5, all without distilling from any proprietary model.</p>
  </div>
  <div lang="zh">
    <h2>语音摘要：PerceptionLM——无需黑箱蒸馏的开放视频理解</h2>
    <p>PerceptionLM（PLM）是Meta FAIR开发的完全开放、可复现的视觉语言模型，专注于图像与视频理解。与大多数依赖GPT-4o等专有模型标注训练数据（即蒸馏）的竞争模型不同，PLM完全基于开源数据和透明方法构建，使科学进展可衡量。</p>
    <p>核心发现是：合成数据扩展对标准视频任务效果良好，但对细粒度视频理解几乎无效——幂律指数为−0.03，而标准任务为−0.15，差距达五倍。为填补这一空白，作者发布了240万条人工标注的细粒度视频问答对（PLM-FGQA），涵盖动作方向、计数、空间关系等现有数据集严重缺失的问题类型。同时发布PLM-STC——47.6万条时空字幕，配合masklet（像素级分割掩码）追踪视频中的目标，实现空间和时间定位。最终PLM-8B在新基准PLM-VideoBench上达到55.6分，超越GPT-4o的51.6分和InternVL2.5的38.5分，且全程未使用任何专有模型蒸馏。</p>
